        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Chapter 2: Bethesda Classification & Surgical Indications",
          "size": 16.0,
          "top": 79.31200000000001,
          "bbox": [
            60.0,
            79.31200000000001,
            496.5600000000001,
            95.31200000000001
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Fine-Needle Aspiration Biopsy (FNAB) results are standardized using the Bethesda System for Reporting Thyroid Cytopathology. Each category corresponds to a specific Risk of Malignancy (ROM) and clinical management directive.",
          "size": 10.0,
          "top": 106.07000000000005,
          "bbox": [
            60.0,
            106.07000000000005,
            552.0,
            144.07000000000005
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "subheading",
          "text": "Bethesda Category IV (Follicular Neoplasm / Suspicious for Follicular Neoplasm):",
          "size": 10.0,
          "top": 162.07000000000005,
          "bbox": [
            60.0,
            162.07000000000005,
            446.76999999999987,
            172.07000000000005
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list-item",
          "text": "• Risk of Malignancy (ROM): Estimated at 25–40%.",
          "size": 10.0,
          "top": 176.07000000000005,
          "bbox": [
            60.0,
            176.07000000000005,
            290.07,
            186.07000000000005
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list-item",
          "text": "• Surgical Requirement: A surgical lobectomy is required to obtain a definitive diagnostic determination.",
          "size": 10.0,
          "top": 190.07000000000005,
          "bbox": [
            60.0,
            190.07000000000005,
            527.9599999999999,
            200.07000000000005
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list-item",
          "text": "• Clinical Rationale: Cytology alone cannot distinguish between a benign follicular adenoma and a malignant follicular thyroid carcinoma. Definitive diagnosis requires histopathology demonstrating vascular or capsular invasion, which cannot be evaluated on FNAB cytology alone. Therefore, clinical observation is insufficient.",
          "size": 10.0,
          "top": 204.07000000000005,
          "bbox": [
            60.0,
            204.07000000000005,
            551.9999999999999,
            242.07000000000005
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "subheading",
          "text": "Bethesda System Category & ROM Summary Table",
          "size": 12.0,
          "top": 272.48400000000004,
          "bbox": [
            60.0,
            272.48400000000004,
            351.4080000000001,
            284.484
          ]
        },
