        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Chapter 3: Therapeutic Interventions & Targeted Therapies",
          "size": 16.0,
          "top": 79.31200000000001,
          "bbox": [
            60.0,
            79.31200000000001,
            507.2160000000002,
            95.31200000000001
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Management of thyroid nodules is tailored according to pathological diagnosis, nodule composition, and clinical stage.",
          "size": 10.0,
          "top": 106.07000000000005,
          "bbox": [
            60.0,
            106.07000000000005,
            551.9999980000002,
            130.07000000000005
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list-item",
          "text": "1. Non-Surgical Ablation Procedures for Benign Nodules: For benign nodules that are symptomatic or cosmetically disturbing, non-surgical minimally invasive techniques offer high efficacy:",
          "size": 10.0,
          "top": 148.07000000000005,
          "bbox": [
            60.0,
            148.07000000000005,
            552.0000040000002,
            186.07000000000005
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list-item",
          "text": "• Percutaneous Ethanol Ablation (PEA): The procedure of choice for predominantly cystic benign nodules.",
          "size": 10.0,
          "top": 190.07000000000005,
          "bbox": [
            60.0,
            190.07000000000005,
            545.6999999999999,
            200.07000000000005
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list-item",
          "text": "• Radiofrequency Ablation (RFA): Preferred thermal ablation modality for solid benign thyroid nodules.",
          "size": 10.0,
          "top": 204.07000000000005,
          "bbox": [
            60.0,
            204.07000000000005,
            529.54,
            214.07000000000005
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list-item",
          "text": "2. Targeted Systemic Therapy for Well-Differentiated Thyroid Carcinoma (DTC): In advanced, progressive, or radioiodine-refractory well-differentiated thyroid carcinoma, multikinase inhibitor targeted drugs are indicated:",
          "size": 10.0,
          "top": 232.07000000000005,
          "bbox": [
            60.0,
            232.07000000000005,
            552.000003,
            270.07000000000005
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list-item",
          "text": "• Sorafenib: Oral multikinase inhibitor targeted for advanced progressive DTC.",
          "size": 10.0,
          "top": 274.07000000000005,
          "bbox": [
            60.0,
            274.07000000000005,
            405.11000000000007,
            284.07
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list-item",
          "text": "• Lenvatinib: Oral multikinase inhibitor demonstrating significant progression-free survival benefits in refractory DTC.",
          "size": 10.0,
          "top": 288.07,
          "bbox": [
            60.0,
            288.07,
            548.4999969999999,
            312.07
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "image": "reading-7-1.png",
          "sha256": "bd888b9479d5d10db8fe55c383170eff5fb9fb50635ec69ef44361f26433fc55",
          "width": 1081,
          "height": 460,
          "text": "",
