        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Executive Summary & Clinical Takeaways",
          "size": 16.0,
          "top": 79.31200000000001,
          "bbox": [
            60.0,
            79.31200000000001,
            378.3680000000001,
            95.31200000000001
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list-item",
          "text": "1. Initial Laboratory Evaluation: Always check baseline serum FT4 and sensitive TSH (TSHs).",
          "size": 10.0,
          "top": 106.07000000000005,
          "bbox": [
            60.0,
            106.07000000000005,
            484.56,
            116.07000000000005
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list-item",
          "text": "2. USG Technical Standard: Use high-frequency ultrasound transducers (10–15 MHz) for thyroid imaging.",
          "size": 10.0,
          "top": 130.07000000000005,
          "bbox": [
            60.0,
            130.07000000000005,
            533.4999999999998,
            140.07000000000005
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list-item",
          "text": "3. Avoid Artifact Misinterpretation: Do not mistake comet tail artifacts or cyst wall foci for punctate echogenic foci (PEF). PEF adds 3 points and falsely elevates TR2 to TR4.",
          "size": 10.0,
          "top": 154.07000000000005,
          "bbox": [
            60.0,
            154.07000000000005,
            551.9999999999995,
            178.07000000000005
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list-item",
          "text": "4. Bethesda IV Surgical Mandate: Follicular neoplasms carry a 25–40% ROM; surgical lobectomy is required for histopathological vascular/capsular evaluation.",
          "size": 10.0,
          "top": 192.07000000000005,
          "bbox": [
            60.0,
            192.07000000000005,
            552.0000059999998,
            216.07000000000005
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list-item",
          "text": "5. Minimally Invasive Ablation: Utilize Percutaneous Ethanol Ablation (PEA) for cystic benign nodules and Radiofrequency Ablation (RFA) for solid benign nodules.",
          "size": 10.0,
          "top": 230.07000000000005,
          "bbox": [
            60.0,
            230.07000000000005,
            551.9999979999998,
            254.07000000000005
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list-item",
          "text": "6. Targeted Therapeutics: Administer multikinase inhibitors Sorafenib or Lenvatinib for advanced, radioiodine-refractory well-differentiated thyroid carcinoma.",
          "size": 10.0,
          "top": 268.07000000000005,
          "bbox": [
            60.0,
            268.07000000000005,
            551.9999999999999,
            292.07
          ]
        },
